  "answer_text": "The **G-Wagon** (also known as the **G-Class**) is a **luxury SUV (Sport Utility Vehicle)** made by **Mercedes-Benz**. Here's a quick overview:\n\n- **Full Name:** The G-Wagen is short for *\"Gel\u00e4ndewagen,\"* which means \"off-road vehicle\" in German.\n\n- **Origins:** When the Mercedes-Benz G-Class was first introduced in 1979, it was not the luxury SUV many associate with it today \u2014 it was a purpose-built off-road vehicle, developed with military applications in mind.\n\n- **Evolution:** Over the years, the G-Class has evolved from a pure utility vehicle into one of the most sought-after luxury SUVs on the market.\n\n- **Design:** From the ground up, the G-Class is engineered to make a statement with its iconic boxy silhouette, sophisticated ladder-frame construction, and advanced all-wheel-drive systems with three locking differentials.\n\n- **Today:** The G-Wagon is a long-standing combination of luxury and off-roading thrills, and it's also a practical city SUV, as its refined mechanics and boxy form make it easy to operate in confined spaces.\n\n- **Electric Version:** In 2024, the G-Class entered a new era with the introduction of the G 580 with EQ Technology, marking its official transition into the world of electric vehicles.\n\nIn summary, the G-Wagon is a **high-end, luxury off-road SUV** that blends rugged capability with premium comfort, and is manufactured by Mercedes-Benz.",
